a256\": \"84a90f703ef37f08840a8f9d896a0df26ba0d006d18afeaeaba10144764814bd\"}, \"matrix_limits\": [\"Staff technical roster is fixed; withdrawal disables launch but no rejoin is offered/allowed for that carrier. This does not qualify World rejoin at runtime. Outsider owner receives read only and no join/ready/start permission.\", \"Ancillary Staff prepare tool remains a one-shot preparation path; ordinary existing one-click simulator unchanged. Recurring authoring/scenes are not qualified by this review.\", \"Closed/ongoing actual mission UI, provider dispatch, full played start/abort/closure and actor resource isolation require the planned real protected Staff cases; none were executed in source review.\"], \"qualification\": {\"source\": \"PASSED_STATIC_0_0_0\", \"runtime\": \"NOT_RUN\", \"world_release\": \"NOT_QUALIFIED\", \"root_installer\": \"NOT_REVIEWED\", \"recovery_material\": \"NOT_REVIEWED\"}, \"schema_version\": \"mission-party-source-counterreview/4\", \"closed_findings\": [{\"id\": \"PARTY-UI-P1-A\", \"reason\": \"Authoritative resolver under the same request lock distinguishes committed from fenced rejected_no_commit; committed result binds actor/mode/source/location/fingerprint before current gate/presence validation. Absent artifacts are checked before inserting the existing native rejection tombstone. Constructor checks that tombstone under same lock before creating carrier. Thus late constructor after resolver cannot commit; existing committed preparation is replayed rather than canceled. UI validates exact resolution DTO, archives exact prior raw journal plus resolution under immutable per-request key, retains old active key until a later explicit new Prepare, and does not rekey on uncertainty. Browser Web Locks plus captured intent/request identity prevent stale tabs from implicitly creating new attempts.\", \"result\": \"CLOSED_STATIC\"}, {\"id\": \"PARTY-SOURCE-P1-A\", \"reason\": \"Staff Event42 location proof uses g.location_id; no undeclar